MQTT Notes

Mosquitto - free open source mqtt broker for windows and linux
you can use broker/server or websockets
we'll write client scripts that send data back and forth, but then there will need to be a launch script that starts all those scripts on boot
use paho-mqtt library to write client scripts in python (mosquitto has options for C, but paho seems more supported)
wrote publisher and subscriber test scripts. remember python virtual environment
"source mqtt-env/bin/activate" in the projects folder

we have working controller reader and subscriber
there was some trouble with controller discovery because of user groups and module loading. I ran "echo joydev | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/joydev.conf" to fix on startup
single version of that command was "sudo modprobe joydev"
